# 6. Authentication vs Authorization ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

These concepts are related but different.

## Authentication

Answers:

> Who are you?

Examples:

```text
SSO
Identity Provider
Service Identity
```

## Authorization

Answers:

> What are you allowed to do?

Examples:

```text
Create Experiment
Log Run
Register Model
Promote Champion
Delete Model Version
```

### Architecture

```text
User / Training Pipeline
          ↓
Authentication
          ↓
Identity Verified
          ↓
Authorization
          ↓
Allowed MLflow Operation
```

### Example Roles

| Role | Responsibilities |
|---|---|
| ML Engineer | Train, log runs, register candidates |
| Model Approver | Review and approve model promotion |
| Release Pipeline | Perform authorized alias updates/deployments |
| Platform Administrator | Operate and maintain MLflow |

### Separation of Duties

A data scientist who registers a candidate should not automatically have unrestricted permission to promote models.

```text
ML Engineer
     ↓
Register Candidate
     ↓
Quality Gates
     ↓
Approval
     ↓
Authorized Release Identity
     ↓
Promote Champion
```

**Important:** Quality gates determine whether a model qualifies for promotion. Authorization determines who may perform the promotion.

The chosen MLflow authentication integration must actually enforce the intended permissions.

