# 8. Observability ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

A healthy MLflow server process does not necessarily mean the entire platform is healthy.

We must monitor the complete dependency chain.

```text
Users / Pipelines
       ↓
Load Balancer
       ↓
MLflow Server
       ↓
PostgreSQL + Artifact Storage
```

### What Should We Monitor?

| Layer | Metrics |
|---|---|
| MLflow API | Availability, request latency, HTTP errors, throughput |
| PostgreSQL | Connections, query latency, locks, replication lag, storage |
| Artifact Store | Upload/download success, latency, 403/5xx errors |
| Registry | Model registration and alias-resolution success |
| Infrastructure | CPU, memory, restarts, saturation |

### Important

Monitoring only:

```text
CPU
Memory
Pod Running
HTTP /health = 200
```

is insufficient.

We must monitor actual operations such as:

```text
Create Experiment
Start Run
Log Metrics
Resolve Champion Alias
Download Model
```

**Mental Model:**

> Monitor whether users can successfully perform the operations the platform promises.

