# 11. Alerting Strategy ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Not every infrastructure metric should trigger a page.

For example:

```text
MLflow CPU = 80%
```

does not automatically mean users are experiencing failures.

We should prioritize user-impacting signals.

### Example Alerts

| Alert | Priority |
|---|---|
| Tracking API sustained failures | High |
| Artifact downloads failing for production models | High |
| Registry alias resolution failing | High |
| PostgreSQL connection exhaustion | High |
| PostgreSQL replication lag | Depends on severity |
| Storage capacity approaching limit | Warning |

### Important Lesson

> Alerts should reflect actionable user impact or credible imminent risk, not arbitrary infrastructure thresholds alone.

