# 18. Accidental Model Artifact Deletion ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

This was one of our Day 5 exercises.

Scenario:

```text
PostgreSQL          Healthy
Registry            Healthy
Champion Alias      Exists
Model Artifact      Deleted
```

### What happens?

The Registry may still show the model version.

However, a new model-loading operation may fail because the artifact is missing.

An inference process that already loaded the model into memory may continue serving until restart or reload.

### Recovery

1. Identify the model version.
2. Locate its artifact URI.
3. Check whether the object was deleted or became inaccessible.
4. Restore from object versioning, protected backup or replica.
5. Verify restored artifact integrity.
6. Load the model.
7. Execute a test prediction.

### Why Restarting MLflow Doesn't Help

Restarting MLflow does not recreate deleted files in external object storage.

**Mental Model:**

> Restarting a healthy application does not repair missing data in an external dependency.

