# 20. Enterprise Architecture Challenge ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Our challenge:

```text
100 ML Engineers
20,000 Training Runs / Month
500 Registered Models
99.9% Availability Target
```

We designed a shared MLflow platform.

## Availability

Use 2–3 MLflow instances behind a load balancer.

Distribute instances across failure domains where possible.

Use shared persistent storage.

## Persistence

Use PostgreSQL with HA/failover capabilities.

Use object storage for model artifacts.

Maintain backups for both.

## Security

Use SSO or an appropriate identity provider.

Apply authorization policies for model registration and promotion.

Protect credentials with secrets management.

Use TLS and network restrictions.

## Observability

Monitor:

```text
Tracking API Success Rate
Registry Operation Success
Artifact Download Success
PostgreSQL Health
```

Define SLIs/SLOs around user-facing operations.

## Disaster Recovery

Restore:

```text
PostgreSQL
Artifacts
Configuration
```

Then validate model loading and inference.

## Upgrades

Test compatibility and migrations in staging.

Back up state before upgrading.

Validate tracking, registry and artifact retrieval after deployment.

