# 21. Common Mistakes

### Mistake 1 — Multiple MLflow Servers Mean Complete HA

Incorrect:

```text
3 MLflow Servers
       ↓
Fully Highly Available
```

Correct:

```text
Application HA
      +
Database HA
      +
Artifact Availability
      +
Network Reliability
```

### Mistake 2 — Health Endpoint Means Everything Works

Incorrect:

```text
/health = 200
      ↓
Platform Healthy
```

Correct:

```text
Tracking Working
Registry Working
Artifact Downloads Working
      ↓
Functional Platform Health
```

### Mistake 3 — PostgreSQL Replication Replaces Backups

Replication helps availability.

Backups help recover lost or corrupted data.

### Mistake 4 — SSO Automatically Enforces All Permissions

Authentication verifies identity.

Authorization must be separately enforced through supported controls and integrations.

### Mistake 5 — Restart MLflow for Every Failure

Not every failure originates in MLflow.

The issue might be:

```text
PostgreSQL
Object Storage
IAM
KMS
Network
Missing Artifact
```

### Mistake 6 — Model Alias Change Automatically Updates Serving

Changing `champion` does not automatically reload a model already in memory.

Deployment/reload mechanisms must apply the change.

### Mistake 7 — Rolling Back the Container Reverses Database Changes

Database migrations may require a separate recovery strategy.

